[[Supportive care]]

Topic outline: managing venous thromboembolism in patients with cancer.

!! Initial assessment
* Thrombosis site, extent, symptoms, and clinical stability.
* Bleeding risk, platelet count, renal and hepatic function, and drug interactions.

!! Anticoagulant selection
* Direct oral anticoagulants and low-molecular-weight heparin.
* Other agents and situations that influence selection.
* Gastrointestinal and genitourinary bleeding risk, absorption, and patient preferences.

!! Duration and follow-up
* Initial treatment and extended anticoagulation.
* Reassessment with changes in cancer activity, treatment, or bleeding risk.
* Recurrent thrombosis during anticoagulation.

!! Special situations
* Thrombocytopenia and active bleeding.
* Brain tumors and intracranial disease.
* Incidental VTE, catheter-associated thrombosis, and unusual-site thrombosis.
* Periprocedural interruption and resumption.

